From 94b60eb29777cc8580159a07b2834de42d83ef95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:24:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] one type scale, one palette that actually ships, nothing
 painted over anything
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Built scripts/check-ui.mjs first, because "the UI looks wrong" is not
actionable and eyes disagree. It measures four things in a real browser
against the production bundle, over six routes x four interactive
surfaces x three viewports:

  SPILL     text painting outside the content box of the nearest ancestor
            that draws a background or border
  OVERLAP   two text-bearing boxes intersecting, so one string is
            painted on top of another
  CONTRAST  every rendered colour against its effective backdrop, by
            WCAG 2.1 ratio
  SCALE     every font-size, weight and family actually rendered

First run: 8 surfaces with defects, 31 spills, 6 real overlaps, 14
contrast failures, 5 font weights.

Getting the measurement right took three passes, and each correction
mattered — acting on the first output would have "fixed" things that
were not broken:

  - a box inside its own ancestor's box is nesting, not collision
  - with a dialog open the page behind it is still in the DOM, and every
    pair across the two layers read as an overlap
  - getBoundingClientRect returns a box for an element an ancestor's
    overflow has clipped away entirely. The Dashboard workload panel is
    max-h-[720px] overflow-auto over 44 rows, so the rows scrolled out
    of it reported boxes intersecting the cards below — 132 "overlaps"
    nobody can see

THE PALETTE WAS NOT SHIPPING
----------------------------
The largest finding, and invisible to every other gate: Tailwind v4
detects sources from this CSS file's own project root, which is
`client/`. Nothing in `shared/` was ever scanned — including
shared/status-appearance.ts, the file that exists so status colour has
one definition.

Measured in the built stylesheet: four of the eight tone backgrounds
were absent — bg-slate-100, bg-amber-100, bg-violet-100, bg-orange-100 —
along with text-amber-800 and text-violet-800. The other four survived
only because they happen to be written a second time somewhere under
client/src. bg-slate-100 computed to rgba(0,0,0,0) in the browser.

Those four tones cover 12,738 of the 15,646 statused review rows, 81 %:
every "nicht erforderlich" (11,947), "offen" (650), "Nachforderung" (97)
and "zurückgestellt" (44) badge rendered with a transparent background,
and where the text colour was missing too, in default near-black. That
is the unstyled pill sitting next to coloured ones in the card grid.

`@source "../../shared"` fixes it. check-ui now reads the built CSS and
asserts every class TONE_APPEARANCE names is present, because nothing
else can catch this: the types compile, the classes are on the elements,
and no tool reports anything.

RENDERING DEFECTS
-----------------
- Project card: two whitespace-nowrap badges in one flex row with no
  min-w-0. A 76-character Projektnummer cannot shrink, so the row grew
  past the card and the number was clipped mid-string — 1,863px² over
  the status badge, 1,526px² into the neighbouring card. Letting both
  shrink made them split the width and BOTH became unreadable
  ("Zustimmun…" beside "G.011800063.01.…"), so they are stacked: the
  status keeps its full label, the number is shown in full.
- Project card had no h-full, so a card whose Station wraps to two lines
  was taller than its neighbour and "Details anzeigen" sat at a
  different height in every column. Now flex-col with mt-auto on the
  footer, a 2-line clamp on the title and on the description, and equal
  grid columns for Projektleiter/Region instead of text-right.
- Gewerke tiles in the project dialog: "Baubetriebstechnologie" is 22
  monospace characters in a half-width tile and painted straight over
  "Baubetriebsplanung"; the Badge ships whitespace-nowrap, so
  "Zustimmung erteilt" ran out of its tile and over the neighbour's. A
  grid item defaults to min-width:auto and refuses to shrink below its
  content — min-w-0 is what lets either wrap at all. That badge also
  still keyed on the raw status.
- Gewerke overview tiles: justify-between with an unshrinkable label
  pushed the count 6-12px past the tile edge on seven tiles at 375px.
- Detail dialog Stammdaten: min-h on the label only sets a floor, so at
  375px "Termin Projektvorstellung" wrapped to three lines and painted
  over "Projektstand". A fixed two-line box cannot grow into a
  neighbour, and it keeps the values on one baseline.
- --muted-foreground was 46.1%: 4.83:1 on white but 4.39:1 on --muted,
  which is where every chip, table header and secondary label sits.
  Below the floor on 13 elements in one wizard step. 44% gives 5.21 and
  4.74; the dark theme already measured 5.81.

TYPOGRAPHY
----------
Five weights rendered (400/500/600/700/900). font-black at 11px with
wide tracking is a smear, not emphasis — 62 occurrences across 11 files
are now font-bold, leaving four weights. Two families, UI and mono, as
intended. Every rendered size already sat on the scale [11 12 14 16 18
20 24 30 36 48 60]; the audit now fails if one drifts off it.

MOBILE
------
The 5-column Fachprüfungen table needed 2.4x the width of a 343px
dialog, so overflow-x did its job and hid Prüfer, Prüfdatum and Kontakt
behind a scroll nothing announced. Below sm each row is now its own
block and each cell carries its column name — all five fields visible,
horizontal scroll measured at 0. Above sm it is an ordinary table.

Result: 31 of 31 surfaces clean, 16 of 16 tone classes in the CSS.
check:ui runs in CI beside the other gates.

Gates: 0 type errors · 145 passed / 6 skipped · 72 lint warnings
(unchanged) · e2e 35/35 · responsive 61/61 · map 6/6 · ui 31/31.
